// Date: 2022-01-05 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547.010
// Description: Bypasses User Account Control using Event Viewer and a relevant Windows Registry modification
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://enigma0x3.net/2016/08/15/fileless-uac-bypass-using-eventvwr-exe-and-registry-hijacking/
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1548.002/T1548.002.md#atomic-test-1---bypass-uac-using-event-viewer-cmd
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_bypass_uac_using_eventviewer.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "_Classes\\mscfile\\shell\\open\\command\\(Default)" and (not(RegistryValueData startswith "%SystemRoot%\\system32\\mmc.exe \"%1\" %"))
